      "requirement": "Check that a fuzz input has at least one byte before reading its first byte.",
      "target_route": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput initializes checksums, then assigns buffSize from data[0], and only afterward tests dataLen < 1.",
      "failure_condition": "For the finite input of length zero, data[0] reads outside the supplied input before the guard can return.",
      "alternative_paths": "The read is unconditional in the complete entry body; no earlier input-length guard or helper intercepts it.",
