        "before": {
          "requirement": "Compile against the former array-based crc32_combine_gen and crc32_combine_op signatures.",
          "applicability": "required",
          "harness_status": "sat",
          "reason": "The old declarations and implementation accept the harness's operator array and two-argument generator call.",
          "source_evidence": [
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-e504b11c2718ebf36516adde",
              "quote": "ZEXTERN void ZEXPORT crc32_combine_gen OF((z_crc_t op[32], z_off_t len2));\n     Generate the operator op corresponding to length len2, to be used with\n   crc32_combine_op(). op must have room for 32 z_crc_t values. (32 is the\n   number of bits in the CRC.)\nZEXTERN uLong ZEXPORT crc32_combine_op OF((uLong crc1, uLong crc2,\n                                           const z_crc_t *op));\n   crc32_combine() if the generated op is used many times."
            },
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-8784829168219a5244b836b6",
              "quote": "void ZEXPORT crc32_combine_gen(op, len2)\n    z_crc_t *op;\n    z_off_t len2;\n{\n    crc32_combine_gen_(op, len2);\n}\n"
            },
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-b96c31111cdc2ebcdb7a1180",
              "quote": "uLong crc32_combine_op(crc1, crc2, op)\n    uLong crc1;\n    uLong crc2;\n    const z_crc_t *op;\n{\n    return gf2_matrix_times(op, crc1) ^ crc2;\n}\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "after": {
          "requirement": "Compile against the changed generator that takes only a length and returns a scalar operator, and pass that scalar to crc32_combine_op.",
          "applicability": "required",
          "harness_status": "unsat",
          "reason": "The unchanged harness supplies two generator arguments and passes an array where the changed operator declaration requires uLong.",
          "source_evidence": [
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-0bee6fadb60fa989232aa848",
              "quote": "ZEXTERN uLong ZEXPORT crc32_combine_gen OF((z_off_t len2));\n     Return the operator corresponding to length len2, to be used with\n   crc32_combine_op().\nZEXTERN uLong ZEXPORT crc32_combine_op OF((uLong crc1, uLong crc2, uLong op));\n   crc32_combine() if the generated op is used more than once."
            },
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-c417ac8b8f04bea4be688d3b",
              "quote": "uLong ZEXPORT crc32_combine_gen(len2)\n    z_off_t len2;\n{\n    return crc32_combine_gen64(len2);\n}\n"
            },
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-e98c995b3409a87c5c8261b2",
              "quote": "uLong crc32_combine_op(crc1, crc2, op)\n    uLong crc1;\n    uLong crc2;\n    uLong op;\n{\n    return multmodp(op, crc1) ^ crc2;\n}\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "same_blocker": "no",
        "reason": "The API mismatch arises after the change; the former API accepts the same harness calls.",
